From: XR1710G Community <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] hwrng: airoha: enable SCU clocks before starting TRNG

The existing Airoha follow-up enables RNG_EN and RNG_OSC_EN before opening
the SCU bus and peripheral clock gates.  On one XR1710G cold boot this raced
the startup health check and the hwrng registration failed with -ENODEV.

Open the required clock gates first, then access and enable the TRNG block.
This is intentionally a minimal ordering change; hardware validation still
requires repeated cold boots on both XR1710G units.

--- a/drivers/char/hw_random/airoha-trng.c
+++ b/drivers/char/hw_random/airoha-trng.c
@@ -92,16 +92,16 @@ static int airoha_trng_init(struct hwrng
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	val = readl(trng->base + TRNG_NS_SEK_AND_DAT_EN);
-	val |= RNG_EN | RNG_OSC_EN;
-	writel(val, trng->base + TRNG_NS_SEK_AND_DAT_EN);
-
 	if (trng->scu) {
 		regmap_set_bits(trng->scu, REG_SCU_BUS_CLK_GAT, SCU_TRNG_BUS_EN);
 		regmap_set_bits(trng->scu, REG_SCU_PER_CLK_GAT_1, SCU_TRNG_PER1_EN);
 		regmap_set_bits(trng->scu, REG_SCU_PER_CLK_GAT_2, SCU_TRNG_PER2_EN);
 	}
 
+	val = readl(trng->base + TRNG_NS_SEK_AND_DAT_EN);
+	val |= RNG_EN | RNG_OSC_EN;
+	writel(val, trng->base + TRNG_NS_SEK_AND_DAT_EN);
+
 	/* Set out of SW Reset */
 	airoha_trng_irq_unmask(trng);
 	writel(0, trng->base + TRNG_HEALTH_TEST_SW_RST);

